// Garrett & DeRouchie chapter vocabulary — GENERATED, do not hand-edit.
//
// Source: the course's own consolidated vocabulary handout for Beginning Hebrew
// (20400WW), covering chapters 2-31 of `A Modern Grammar for Biblical Hebrew`.
// Chapter 1 is not in that handout; its list is hand-curated in `vocabulary.ts`.
//
// Every field here comes from the book: the gloss wording, the gender, the
// construct form, the irregular plural, and the per-stem glosses for verbs.
// Nothing is inferred except `partOfSpeech`, which the book does not print --
// it is read off the gender notation, the stem list, and the gloss.
//
// What is deliberately absent:
//   * `transliteration` -- the handout has none, and inventing ~500 SBL
//     romanizations by hand would bake in errors the data tests cannot catch.
//   * `frequency` -- no counts in the handout either. Real per-lemma counts land
//     with the OSHB pipeline (issue #75); see ROADMAP.md. Both fields are
//     optional on `HebrewVocabWord` for exactly this reason.
//
// The handout carries a small number of typographic errors (a wrong letter, a
// vowel point that contradicts the entry's own construct form). Those are
// corrected here and listed in `CORRECTIONS` below, with the reason, so the
// divergence from the printed page is auditable rather than silent.
//
// PLANNED CHANGE (issue #109): the handout should not be the authority on Hebrew
// orthography -- a retyped Word document is the worst available source for it,
// which is what the CORRECTIONS list below is evidence of. Once the OSHB
// pipeline (#75) exists, `hebrew`, `root`, `partOfSpeech`, `gender` and
// `frequency` come from the Westminster Leningrad Codex, and this file keeps
// only what the handout alone knows: the chapter/category mapping and the gloss
// wording, which is what the chapter quizzes are marked against.
//
// Regenerating: this file was produced by a one-time extraction from the .docx.
// The handout is course material and is not in the repo; re-running the
// extraction means re-running it against your own copy.

// `gd` comes from vocabulary-types, not textbooks: textbooks.ts reads the
// merged vocabulary at module scope, so importing it from there would make this
// file part of a cycle and `gd` would be undefined when these literals evaluate.
import { gd, type HebrewVocabWord } from './vocabulary-types';

